// Canonical sources: a body that carries control keeps the value it stood
// on. The loop's last assignment and the if's own leave x at 7 as the
// standing value; the choose after them can only fail, so the body stops
// there, the return never runs, and the body answers 7.
// Answer: 7.
int x = 0;
int n = 3;
while (n > 0) { n = n - 1; x = x + 2; }
if (x > 2) { x = x + 1; }
choose { fail; } , { fail; }
return x + 100;
